    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2mk7g4v",
      "content": "Community Health Nursing focuses on the health of populations and communities rather than individuals alone. It emphasizes disease prevention, health promotion, environmental sanitation, maternal and child health, immunization, and national health programs. In nursing competitive examinations such as RRB Nursing, questions frequently come from levels of prevention, primary health care, immunization schedules, national health programs, and the role of community health nurses."
    },
